;; The whole boundary for mesh_llm_answer.kotoba. `:llm/infer` is a KIND-level
;; grant and there is deliberately no :kotoba.policy/capability-resources entry
;; beside it: the guest supplies only a prompt, never a destination, so a
;; resource scope here would constrain the guest's own payload rather than
;; where the call goes. A node that wants a narrower boundary narrows the
;; :llm-client it injects at `kotoba.mesh.node/start!`.
;;
;; Note what is NOT granted: :graph/kotoba. This guest reaches no kgraph op,
;; and `compile-route`'s check-before-emit would reject it at startup if it
;; tried.
{:kotoba.policy/capabilities #{:llm/infer}}
